  "result": "Perfect! All 204 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n**src/statements.js** - New function:\n\n**statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)** - Generates a customer statement:\n- **Input**: \n  - customerId: normalized to uppercase and trimmed\n  - invoices: array of all invoices to search through\n  - asOf: date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n- **Filtering**:\n  - Includes only invoices for the specified customer\n  - Only invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - Only invoices with issueDate on or before asOf\n- **Sorting**: by issueDate (ascending)\n- **Output**: ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue }) where:\n  - customerId: normalized customer ID\n  - invoices: array with { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n    - total: full invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n    - due: balance still owed (from balanceDue)\n  - totalDue: sum of all due amounts\n- **Error**: CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if customer doesn't exist\n\n**Tests** - 12 new tests covering:\n- Empty statement (no invoices)\n- Single and multiple invoices\n- Filtering by status (draft/paid excluded, issued/partially_paid included)\n- Date filtering (before, on, and after asOf)\n- Correct sorting by issueDate\n- Correct totalDue calculation\n- Customer ID normalization (handles mixed case and spaces)\n- Customer filtering (only that customer's invoices)\n\nThe implementation provides a complete statement view of a customer's outstanding invoices with proper filtering, sorting, and balance calculations.",
